BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:robots-agents-future-of-work-fribourg-2026@swissdataevents.ch
DTSTAMP:20261107T114104Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Zurich:20261209T163000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Zurich:20261209T183000
SUMMARY:Robots\, Agents and the Future of Work
LOCATION:Université de Fribourg\, Campus de Pérolles\, PER 21\, Boulevard
  de Pérolles 90
DESCRIPTION:A panel with Peter Fankhauser (co-founder and CEO of ANYbotics)
  and Anne Scherer (co-founder of Delta Labs) on how AI is changing company
  operations\, from autonomous robots on the plant floor to generative AI i
 n the boardroom.\n\nOrganiser: University of Fribourg (CSIS)\n\nDetails an
 d registration: https://swissdataevents.ch/events/robots-agents-future-of-
 work-fribourg-2026/
URL:https://swissdataevents.ch/events/robots-agents-future-of-work-fribourg
 -2026/
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:epi-winterschool-generative-ai-wengen-2027@swissdataevents.ch
DTSTAMP:20261107T114104Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270124
SUMMARY:Generative AI for Epidemiology Researchers: Practical Skills and Re
 sponsible Use
LOCATION:Wengen\, Bernese Oberland\, Wengen (Bern)
DESCRIPTION:A three-day course in Wengen on using generative AI responsibly
  in research\, pairing lectures with computer practicals on analysis\, lit
 erature searching\, scientific writing\, study websites and agentic AI —
  and on where error\, bias and reproducibility break down.\n\nOrganiser: S
 wiss Epidemiology Winter School\n\nDetails and registration: https://swiss
 dataevents.ch/events/epi-winterschool-generative-ai-wengen-2027/
URL:https://swissdataevents.ch/events/epi-winterschool-generative-ai-wengen
 -2027/
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sdsc-connect-environmental-sciences-bern-2027@swissdataevents.ch
DTSTAMP:20261107T114104Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Zurich:20270203T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Zurich:20270203T163000
SUMMARY:SDSC-Connect: Connecting Digital Environmental Sciences
LOCATION:Central Bern venue to be announced
DESCRIPTION:A day in Bern on making environmental data usable across discip
 lines and institutions — data access and sharing\, data infrastructure\,
  and the role of machine learning and AI across climate\, ecology\, hydrol
 ogy\, the cryosphere\, natural hazards and agriculture\, with keynotes\, i
 nvited talks\, break-outs and a poster fair. Seats are limited and the ven
 ue is still to be announced.\n\nOrganiser: Swiss Data Science Center\n\nDe
 tails and registration: https://swissdataevents.ch/events/sdsc-connect-env
 ironmental-sciences-bern-2027/
URL:https://swissdataevents.ch/events/sdsc-connect-environmental-sciences-b
 ern-2027/
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
